            {"id": "b", "text": "Hyper-Threading Manager in Windows Task Manager, which manually assigns P-cores to specific applications", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. There is no 'Hyper-Threading Manager' in Windows Task Manager. Task Manager's CPU affinity setting allows manual thread pinning to specific logical processors, but this is not a feature designed for hybrid CPU thread scheduling. Manual affinity is a workaround, not the designed solution."},
            {"id": "c", "text": "AMD's Simultaneous Multi-Threading (SMT) controller, which dynamically assigns workloads based on core temperature", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. AMD SMT is AMD's implementation of hyperthreading; it is irrelevant to Intel's hybrid architecture and Thread Director. AMD's Zen architecture does not use P-core/E-core hybrid designs (though AMD does have 3D V-Cache variants with performance differentiation)."},
