            {"id": "b", "text": "USB 3.2 Gen 2x2 cable (20 Gbps)", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. USB 3.2 Gen 2x2 operates at 20 Gbps (2 lanes × 10 Gbps). This is below the 40 Gbps threshold required by the question. USB4 Gen 3x2 (40 Gbps) would meet the threshold, but USB 3.2 Gen 2x2 does not."},
            {"id": "c", "text": "InfiniBand HDR cable (200 Gbps)", "correct": True, "rationale": "Correct. InfiniBand HDR (High Data Rate) operates at 200 Gbps (HDR100 per port at 100 Gbps, HDR at 200 Gbps). Widely used in HPC (High-Performance Computing) clusters and data centers for low-latency, high-bandwidth interconnects. This far exceeds 40 Gbps."},
            {"id": "d", "text": "DisplayPort 1.4 cable (25.92 Gbps raw bandwidth)", "correct": False, "rationale": "Incorrect. DisplayPort 1.4 HBR3 has a raw data rate of 8.1 Gbps per lane × 4 lanes = 32.4 Gbps, with effective bandwidth of approximately 25.92 Gbps after 8b/10b encoding. This is below the 40 Gbps threshold. DisplayPort 2.1 (UHBR10: 40 Gbps, UHBR20: 80 Gbps) would meet the threshold, but DP 1.4 does not."},
